P1
  Change: every reply is walked iteratively as it is read off the wire,
          before any decode, and refused with ErrorKind::InvalidResponse
          when a path through it nests too deep. bson decodes nested
          documents recursively, so a hostile server's deep reply otherwise
          overflows the stack and aborts the process.
          MAX_REPLY_DEPTH = 32 bounds every part the driver decodes with
          serde or TryFrom ($clusterTime, error bodies, hello, auth, plain
          run_command replies). In a debug build the serde decode costs about
          24 KiB of stack per level, so 32 levels fit a 2 MiB thread with
          over 2x margin; real servers nest these parts a few levels deep.
          MAX_BATCH_DEPTH = 256, counted from the reply root, bounds the
          documents of cursor.firstBatch and cursor.nextBatch, which the
          cursor operations keep raw; it admits a stored document nested 200
          deep under its three wrapper levels.
          RawCommandResponse::body and RunCommand::handle_response decode the
          whole body, batches included, so they re-walk it at 32 everywhere.
  Files: src/cmap/conn/wire/message.rs, src/cmap/conn/command.rs,
         src/operation/run_command.rs
  Upstream: none filed (project rule: own issue and local workaround)

